<h3>3. How to Upload Documentation</h3>
<p>Uploads are handled through the spending-account documentation portal. Your session is pre-linked to
this notice — no member login is required for flagged-claim receipts:</p>

<p style="text-align:center;margin:18px 0">
<a href="https://mymeridian-receipts.example/docupload?m=MHP-40218773&amp;grace=2026" style="display:inline-block;background:#00695C;color:#fff;padding:12px 40px;text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px;font-weight:bold">Upload Flagged-Claim Receipts</a>
</p>
<p style="font-size:13px;color:#666;text-align:center">Portal address: https://www.mymeridian.com/members/fsa/documentation</p>

<h3>4. Acceptable Documentation</h3>
<ul>
<li>Itemized receipt or provider statement (date, service, amount, provider name)</li>
<li>For OTC items: pharmacy printout plus prescribing provider confirmation (entered on the portal form)</li>
<li>EOB is acceptable where the claim was partially adjudicated</li>
</ul>
<p style="font-size:13px;background:#FFFDE7;padding:10px">A year-end benefits email asking for receipts is exactly the kind of message that fraud teams warn
about — and your suspicion is appropriate. Two things distinguish this notice: the upload session is scoped
to the three claim IDs above (nothing else can be submitted through it), and no card number, SSN, or login
credential is requested anywhere in the flow. The deadline, however, is set by the IRS grace-period rule,
not by our processing schedule.</p>

<h3>5. Timeline &amp; Forfeiture</h3>
<ul>
<li>Documentation deadline: <b>before year end</b> (grace period statutory close)</li>
<li>Claims resolved within 5 business days of upload; reimbursement to your direct-deposit account on file</li>
<li>Unresolved balance at 1 Jan 2027: forfeited to the plan (not recoverable; reported on your 2027 W-2 summary)</li>
</ul>

